# Deep-Guard Fix — 2026-07-10T20:05:28+03:30
# File: /tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js  Line: 128  Severity: high
# Type: xss

## Root Cause
The error message `err` can contain untrusted user input, leading to potential XSS attacks when rendered in the response.

## Explanation
The patch modifies the code to escape or encode the error message before passing it to `req.flash`. This prevents any malicious script in the error message from being executed in the browser, thereby mitigating the XSS vulnerability.

## Patch
--- a/tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js
+++ b/tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js
@@ -127,6 +127,7 @@
             }
         }).catch(err => {
             output = {
                 product: product
+                error: escapeHtml(err) // use an HTML escaping function
             }
             req.flash('danger', escapeHtml(err));
             res.render('app/modifyproduct', {
                 output: output
             });
         })

